From 0cd16ad76273f920b36c06005369fd1324f3ba12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:36:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): sidebar row shows the background processes
 holding it off green, with Stop [daveey]

A finished chat held un-green for ~24 h by a 72 h tap watcher showed nothing
on its row to say why. The backend now stamps background_processes (id,
redacted/truncated command, started_at, pid; oldest first) next to
background_active, and the row renders a process glyph beside the kanban
badge (count when >1). Hover lists each command with its age and a Stop
button; click opens the session.

Stop posts /api/sessions/{id}/background-processes/{proc}/stop, which kills
via process_registry.kill_process (the process_manage kill path) when this
backend supervises it, else terminates the start-time-checked pid of a
process another Hermes process owns. Ownership is checked against the row's
lineage ids; the stamp cache is dropped so the row goes green at once.
